# A BallVector with one-limb centers times a positive power of two c (milestone2.md, "BallVector":
# bv_mul_pow2_k; "Scaling a ball by a power of two"): exact when nothing underflows, so that halving a
# polynomial again and again adds nothing to its radius. The centers by mul_pow2_step_1, entry by
# entry, with the mask that each was scaled exactly (bv_mul_pow2_step_1), and-ed into the state's ex;
# the state's m and ok those of norm_upper_1 on the centers written; the one radius bv_mul_pow2_radius,
# c rx when every entry and the radius were scaled exactly, otherwise the second number after RN(c rx):
# the largest of the radii of ball_mul_pow2_1 entry by entry. norm_finish_1 tests it: when it is not
# finite (the operand is the whole space, or a center or the radius overflowed), every center written
# is zero and the radius +infinity, the whole space.
fold:          bv_mul_pow2_1
arrays:        stored x
scalars:       stored rx, supplied c
state:         m, mask ok, mask ex
step:          (z, e) = bv_mul_pow2_step_1(x, c)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_1(m, ok, z)
record:        ex = and(ex, e)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
combine:       ex = and(ex, ex)
radius:        rz = bv_mul_pow2_radius(m, ex, rx, c)
finish:        (r, finite) = norm_finish_1(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z
output:        r
output:        mask finite
value:         x*c
requires:      ball_vector x rx
requires:      power_of_two c
ensures:       encloses_entries z r x*c x=x,rx flag=finite finite_when=abs_le((abs(x)+rx)*c,-2) radii_when=abs_le(rx*c,-2) exact_when=zero_or_abs_gt(x*c,eta/(2*u));zero_or_abs_gt(rx*c,eta/(2*u))
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/BvPow2.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBvPow2.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        mul_pow2_step_1 on the centers, the radius of ball_mul_pow2_1 with the exactness of every entry (milestone2.md, BallVector)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
